import DocsApiTable from './DocsApiTable.astro';
---
  <p>Read and write these properties on the effect instance. Writes are immediately readable and render on the next frame without recapturing the target.</p>
  <DocsApiTable label="Writable effect controls">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Property</th><th scope="col">Type</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row"><code>time</code><p>Effect time in seconds. Supports forward and backward seeking, including negative time.</p></th><td><code>number</code></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row"><code>intensity</code><p>Effect strength, clamped to 0–1 after validation. It is not a universal height or opacity setting.</p></th><td><code>number</code></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </DocsApiTable>
  <p>Both values must be finite and representable as float32. Give direct writes, a timeline or another animation driver responsibility for these controls.</p>
